   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* --- Liouville: Hamiltonian flows are volume-preserving --- */\ndepends(HH, zs)$\nXHl : makelist( if k <= 3 then diff(HH, ps[k]) else -diff(HH, qs[k-3]),\n                k, 1, 6)$\ndivX : ratsimp( sum( diff(XHl[k], zs[k]), k, 1, 6) )$\nprint(\"LIOUVILLE.  For a completely generic H(q,p):\")$\nprint(\"   X_H = \", XHl)$\nprint(\"   div X_H = Σ ∂(X_H)^k/∂z^k = \", divX)$\nprint(\"   The mixed partials cancel in pairs: ∂²H/∂q∂p from the q-block\")$\nprint(\"   against −∂²H/∂p∂q from the p-block.  Phase-space volume is\")$\nprint(\"   conserved by EVERY Hamiltonian flow, whatever H is.\")$\nremove(HH, dependency)$\n\n/* --- flows are symplectic, not isometric --- */\nOm2 : matrix([0,-1],[1,0])$\nsymp_check(Mt, label) := block([S],\n  S : ratsimp( trigsimp( transpose(Mt) . Om2 . Mt - Om2 ) ),\n  print(\"   \", label),\n  print(\"      M = \", Mt),\n  print(\"      MᵀΩM − Ω = \", S, \"     det M = \",\n        ratsimp(trigsimp(determinant(Mt)))) )$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"SYMPLECTIC, NOT ISOMETRIC.  Jacobians of the time-t flow map:\")$\n/* harmonic oscillator H = (p² + q²)/2 :  q = q₀cos t + p₀sin t, etc. */\nsymp_check( matrix([cos(tv), sin(tv)],[-sin(tv), cos(tv)]),\n            \"harmonic oscillator, H = (p² + q²)/2\")$\n/* free particle H = p²/2 :  q = q₀ + p₀t,  p = p₀ */\nsymp_check( matrix([1, tv],[0, 1]),\n            \"free particle, H = p²/2\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"Both preserve ω and both have determinant 1, so both preserve AREA.\")$\nprint(\"But the free-particle map is a shear: a round blob of initial\")$\nprint(\"conditions becomes a long thin sliver, of the same area.  No metric\")$\nprint(\"survives the flow; only the area does.  Phase space has no notion\")$\nprint(\"of length or angle to lose.\")$\n\n/* a NON-Hamiltonian flow, for contrast */\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"CONTRAST: the damped oscillator q̇ = p, ṗ = −q − 2γp.\")$\nXdamp : [pp, -qq - 2*gam*pp]$\nprint(\"   div X = \", ratsimp( diff(Xdamp[1], qq) + diff(Xdamp[2], pp) ),\n      \"   ≠ 0 for γ > 0\")$\nprint(\"   Volume shrinks at the rate e^{−2γt}: trajectories collapse onto\")$\nprint(\"   an attractor.  That cannot happen in a Hamiltonian system, and\")$\nprint(\"   the obstruction is exactly div X_H = 0 above.  Damping is not a\")$\nprint(\"   force one can put in H; it is a statement that the system is not\")$\nprint(\"   closed.\")$",
