   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* --- Angular momentum: so(3) as functions on phase space --- */\nLL1 : q2*p3 - q3*p2$\nLL2 : q3*p1 - q1*p3$\nLL3 : q1*p2 - q2*p1$\nLv  : [LL1, LL2, LL3]$\neps(i,j,k) := (j-i)*(k-i)*(k-j)/2$\n\nprint(\"angular momentum L = q × p, as three functions on phase space:\")$\nprint(\"   {Lᵢ,Lⱼ} − ε_ijk Lₖ :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:i+1 thru 3 do block([k], k : 6-i-j,\n  print(\"      i=\", i, \" j=\", j, \" : \", ratsimp( pb(Lv[i],Lv[j])\n                                                 - eps(i,j,k)*Lv[k] )))$\nprint(\"   The SAME structure constants as so(3) in 5.01 — where they were\")$\nprint(\"   matrices, and in 1.01, where they were the cross product.  Here\")$\nprint(\"   they are functions, and the bracket is Poisson's.  One algebra,\")$\nprint(\"   three incarnations.\")$\n\n/* Conservation under ANY central Hamiltonian.\n   NOTE: gradef is needed.  Without it Maxima leaves 'diff(Vgen(r), q2)\n   unevaluated instead of applying the chain rule, and the brackets below\n   print as non-zero expressions that happen to cancel. */\ngradef(Vgen(xx), Vp(xx))$\nrn : sqrt(q1^2 + q2^2 + q3^2)$\nHcent : (p1^2 + p2^2 + p3^2)/2 + Vgen(rn)$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"for ANY central Hamiltonian H = |p|²/2 + V(|q|) :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do\n  print(\"   {L\", i, \", H} = \", radcan( pb(Lv[i], Hcent) ))$\nprint(\"   Rotational symmetry ⟹ angular momentum conserved.  That is\")$\nprint(\"   Noether's theorem, and geometrically it is one line: the flow of\")$\nprint(\"   Lᵢ preserves H, so H's flow preserves Lᵢ.  Antisymmetry of the\")$\nprint(\"   bracket does the work.\")$\n\n/* --- Kepler: an extra conserved vector --- */\nkk : k$\nHkep : (p1^2 + p2^2 + p3^2)/2 - kk/rn$\ncrossv(a,b) := [ a[2]*b[3]-a[3]*b[2], a[3]*b[1]-a[1]*b[3],\n                 a[1]*b[2]-a[2]*b[1] ]$\npv : [p1,p2,p3]$  qv : [q1,q2,q3]$\nAv : crossv(pv, Lv) - kk*qv/rn$          /* Laplace–Runge–Lenz */\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"KEPLER, H = |p|²/2 − k/|q|.  The Laplace–Runge–Lenz vector\")$\nprint(\"   A = p × L − k q/|q| :\")$\nprint(\"   A₁ = \", Av[1])$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   {Aᵢ, H} :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do\n  print(\"      i = \", i, \" : \", radcan( pb(Av[i], Hkep) ))$\nprint(\"   Conserved — and NOT a consequence of rotational symmetry, since\")$\nprint(\"   it is a vector independent of L.  Kepler's problem has a hidden\")$\nprint(\"   symmetry that a general central force does not.\")$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   {Lᵢ, Aⱼ} − ε_ijk Aₖ :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:1 thru 3 do\n  if i < j then block([k_], k_ : 6-i-j,\n    print(\"      i=\", i, \" j=\", j, \" : \",\n          radcan( pb(Lv[i], Av[j]) - eps(i,j,k_)*Av[k_] )))$\nprint(\"      (so A transforms as a vector under rotations, as it must)\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   {Aᵢ, Aⱼ} + 2H ε_ijk Lₖ :\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:i+1 thru 3 do block([k_], k_ : 6-i-j,\n  print(\"      i=\", i, \" j=\", j, \" : \",\n        radcan( pb(Av[i], Av[j]) + 2*Hkep*eps(i,j,k_)*Lv[k_] )))$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"On a bound energy shell H = E < 0, rescaling A by 1/√(−2E) turns\")$\nprint(\"that last line into {Ãᵢ,Ãⱼ} = ε_ijk Lₖ.  Together with {L,L} and\")$\nprint(\"{L,Ã} the six functions close into so(4) — a bigger symmetry than\")$\nprint(\"the rotations one can see.\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"THAT is why Kepler orbits close.  The extra conserved vector points\")$\nprint(\"along the major axis and pins it in place, so the ellipse cannot\")$\nprint(\"precess.  6.02 added one term, −2ML²/r³, to the effective potential;\")$\nprint(\"it breaks the hidden symmetry, A is no longer conserved, and the\")$\nprint(\"axis drifts by 6πM/(a(1−e²)) per orbit.  Mercury's 43″ per century\")$\nprint(\"is the measurement of a broken symmetry.\")$",
