   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* --- Darboux: no local invariants --- */\n/* In two dimensions EVERY nowhere-zero 2-form is closed automatically\n   (there are no 3-forms), so every area form is symplectic.  Darboux says\n   coordinates always exist in which it is exactly dP ∧ dQ.  Here is one\n   case done explicitly. */\ndeclare([xx, yy], real)$\ndens : exp(xx)$                       /* ω = e^x dx ∧ dy */\nXn : exp(xx)$  Yn : yy$\nJd : matrix([diff(Xn,xx), diff(Xn,yy)],\n            [diff(Yn,xx), diff(Yn,yy)])$\nprint(\"DARBOUX, explicitly, in two dimensions.\")$\nprint(\"   ω = \", dens, \" dx ∧ dy\")$\nprint(\"   try X = \", Xn, \",  Y = \", Yn)$\nprint(\"   Jacobian = \", Jd, \"   det = \", ratsimp(determinant(Jd)))$\nprint(\"   dX ∧ dY = (det J) dx ∧ dy = \", ratsimp(determinant(Jd)),\n      \" dx ∧ dy\")$\nprint(\"   difference from ω : \", ratsimp( determinant(Jd) - dens ))$\nprint(\"   So in the coordinates (X,Y) the form is exactly dX ∧ dY.\")$\nprint(\"   Any positive density can be flattened the same way — pick X with\")$\nprint(\"   dX/dx equal to the density and leave Y alone.  In 2n dimensions\")$\nprint(\"   the same conclusion holds, by Moser's argument.\")$\n\n/* --- the contrast with Riemannian geometry --- */\n/* NOTE: taking K as a function of an explicit f, rather than declaring\n   depends(f,xx) and substituting afterwards.  Substituting into a noun\n   'diff(f,xx,2) leaves 'diff(sin(xx),xx,2) unevaluated, and neither\n   ev(...,diff) nor ratsimp clears it. */\nKof(fex) := ratsimp( -diff(fex, xx, 2)/fex )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"CONTRAST.  Try the same trick on a METRIC  g = dx² + f(x)² dy².\")$\nprint(\"   K = −f″/f  (3.04, 5.05), a function of the metric alone, so no\")$\nprint(\"   change of coordinates can alter it.  Unless f″ = 0 there are\")$\nprint(\"   therefore NO coordinates making g the identity on a neighbourhood.\")$\nprint(\"      f = sin x  :  K = \", Kof(sin(xx)), \"   the unit sphere\")$\nprint(\"      f = sinh x :  K = \", Kof(sinh(xx)), \"   the hyperbolic plane\")$\nprint(\"      f = x      :  K = \", Kof(xx),\n      \"   the flat plane in polar coordinates (4.04)\")$\nprint(\"   Only the last can be flattened, and 4.04 showed exactly that:\")$\nprint(\"   Γ ≠ 0 there, but R ≡ 0.\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   A metric can be made δᵢⱼ AT A POINT with vanishing first\")$\nprint(\"   derivatives (4.03's normal coordinates), and no further.  The\")$\nprint(\"   second derivatives survive as curvature, and Stage 4 is the study\")$\nprint(\"   of that obstruction.\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   A symplectic form has no obstruction at any order.  Two symplectic\")$\nprint(\"   manifolds of the same dimension are locally indistinguishable —\")$\nprint(\"   there is no symplectic curvature to distinguish them.  Everything\")$\nprint(\"   interesting is therefore GLOBAL: symplectic capacities, Gromov's\")$\nprint(\"   non-squeezing theorem, Floer homology.  It is a topological\")$\nprint(\"   subject wearing geometric clothes.\")$",
